WEBVTT
Kind: captions

00:00:02.825 --> 00:00:06.487 position:63%
Killer whales are opportunistic when
they take fish from long lines.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.503 position:63%
As with most predators, they prefer
easy prey requiring the least effort.

00:00:13.263 --> 00:00:17.006 position:63%
But Jared's tags prove they can
dive to more than half a mile

00:00:17.606 --> 00:00:19.828 position:63%
when they have to hunt without
the help of the fishermen.

00:00:24.128 --> 00:00:27.329 position:63%
Killer whales have proven that they
are capable of adapting to the

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:30.790 position:63%
pressure at these depths, which
is about a hundred times that of

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:36.583 position:63%
atmospheric pressure, thanks to two
incredible physical adaptations.

00:00:37.304 --> 00:00:39.944 position:63%
First, a network of veins called the

00:00:40.184 --> 00:00:43.525 position:63%
retimirabile covers the
brain and major organs.

00:00:44.385 --> 00:00:47.706 position:63%
By filling up with blood, this
compensates for the crushing pressure.

00:00:48.807 --> 00:00:53.288 position:63%
Secondly, their large muscle mass stores
the essential oxygen that they need.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:01.302 position:63%
So efficiently that the killer whales
die with their lungs almost empty.

00:01:06.871 --> 00:01:08.272 position:63%
It's bad news for fishermen.

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:13.234 position:63%
These sleek giants are just as capable
of emptying the lines at the surface

00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:23.388 position:63%
as they are at the bottom.

00:01:39.864 --> 00:01:40.825 position:63%
Dumb killer whales.

00:01:41.506 --> 00:01:42.627 position:63%
They won't let us fish.

